1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Download the APK

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Copy the file to USB

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:28,000
3 · Connect the USB drive to your TV and open your file manager.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:42,000
4 · Select your USB drive and find the folder where you saved the APK.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:56,000
5 · Open HorizonX-3.5.1.apk.

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,700
6 · Select Install. If HorizonX is already installed, you will see Update instead.

7
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:09,700
If Android blocks installation

8
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:23,700
7 · Confirm Install or Update in the Android window.

9
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:29,400
8 · When Android confirms the installation, select Open.

10
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:43,400
9 · In HorizonX, open the Settings gear.

11
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:57,400
10 · In System, select Set up HorizonX.

12
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:03,100
11 · Select TV information.

13
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:12,100
12 · Select Build and press OK seven times to enable Developer options.

14
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:26,100
13 · Return to Set up HorizonX and open Developer options.

15
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:37,267
14 · Enable USB debugging (or ADB debugging, depending on your TV).

16
00:02:37,267 --> 00:02:51,267
15 · Return to HorizonX and select Authorize ADB connection.

17
00:02:51,267 --> 00:03:05,267
16 · If Allow debugging? appears, select Always allow and confirm.

18
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:19,267
17 · Under Use HorizonX as home, select Activate Home.

19
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:33,267
18 · Press Home on your remote: HorizonX should open as your home screen.

20
00:03:33,267 --> 00:03:42,354
Done. Pressing Home will return you to HorizonX.
